.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int dlmulti (char * name, char * file, int flag, void ** libr, const char * fmt,  ...)"
.PP
satisfy symbols from a shared object. 
.PP
dlopen() on steroids. NOIR_SUCC: got all symbols NOIR_PARTIAL: got all required symbols, but not all optional symbols NOIR_NOTFOUND: didn't get all of the required symbols NOIR_FAIL: invalid parameters NOIR_NODATA: caller asked for empty symbol name NOIR_NOFILE: couldn't open shared object NOIR_OOM: out of memory, symbol name too long
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP - a logical name for the library, or NULL 
.br
\fIfile\fP - the shared object; will be dlopen()ed and hence looked for in the usual places for shared objects (defined by ld.so.conf on linux) 
.br
\fIflag\fP - dlopen()-flags (RTLD_*) 
.br
\fIlibr\fP - where to store the handle for the library 
.br
\fIfmt\fP - a space-separated list of symbols to try and load. symbols prefixed by '?' are optional, symbols prefixed by '!' are required. 
.br
\fI...\fP - where to store the function-pointers we get (or NULL for failure on an optional symbol)
.RE
.PP

.SS "char* e2locale (const char * utf8)"
.PP
convert C-string in UTF8 encoding to locale-dependent encoding. 
.PP
\fBReturns:\fP
.RS 4
a locale-dependent string that must be free()d. 
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIutf8\fP - C-string in UTF8 encoding
.RE
.PP

.SS "char* e2utf8 (const char * ascii)"
.PP
